
## --help
rc=0
git.grove.auth.github.set — put a github token on a grove's rack, securely

usage:
  rhx git.grove.auth.github.set <grove> [--mode plan|apply] [--refresh]

options:
  --mode     plan (default) or apply
  --refresh  re-set a slug that already answers (rotated or expired pat)
  --env      keyrack env; default camp
  --owner    keyrack owner; default ehmpath
  --org      org sigil for the slug; default @all (every org reads it)

an ec2 grove only: off ec2 the token lives in os.secure, set on the box.

the value is TYPED on the box over an interactive ssh tty — never passed
as an argument, never sent down a duct. see the header for why.

## a grove with no ec2 identity → refused at rung 0b
rc=2
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; an ec2 grove's IMDS answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      └─ ✋ ConstraintError: grove 'grove-x' has no ec2 identity — IMDS does not answer there

  why: this skill stores the token in aws.params, and only an ec2 box can
       read that vault. a local, house, or hetzner grove would get a value
       it can never read back, written into whatever account its shell holds
  fix: keep the token in os.secure instead — run this ON that grove, at a tty:
    cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup && rhx keyrack set \
      --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN --org @all --env camp --vault os.secure
    (or, on a box with a human: gh auth login)

## the control · an ec2 grove → passes rung 0b, plan only
rc=0
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; an ec2 grove's IMDS answers it)
   └─ drive
      ├─ box  reachable at 'grove-x'
      ├─ ec2  the box holds an instance identity, so aws.params is readable
      ├─ rhx  present
      ├─ rhx  runs (keyrack answered)
      └─ ✔ the rack already answers for GITHUB_TOKEN — no work

🔑 already set!
   ├─ to replace a rotated or expired pat: --refresh
   └─ to prove gh accepts it:
      rhx git.grove.send grove-x --what 'gh auth status'

## a grove that does not answer → rc 1, names the wake
rc=1
🐢 heres the wave...

🔑 git.grove.auth.github.set grove-x --mode plan
   ├─ slug:  owner=ehmpath  @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN
   ├─ vault: aws.params  (central; an ec2 grove's IMDS answers it)
   └─ drive
      └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: grove 'grove-x' does not answer at ssh alias 'grove-x'

  why: the box is asleep, or its tunnel is not bound
  fix: wake it — a wake is idempotent
    rhx git.grove.wake grove-x

## a grove never registered → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: grove 'grove-none' is not registered
   list them: rhx git.grove.list

## no grove named → the usage
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: usage: rhx git.grove.auth.github.set <grove> [--mode apply]
   list them: rhx git.grove.list

